------------------------ ELK Stack -------------------------

- Why we need ELK Stack ?
- Suppose there is 6000 movies in our DB jahan let suppose humne ye search krna ha ke batman movie tu technically hame har rows ko scan krta ha.

- SELECT * FROM MOVIES WHEN NAME = ""%batman%;
- There is one problem here when the data size grows eventually so the response time will also grown as well.
- Response time = also grows

Elastic Company made a solution: Elastic Stack

-----------------  Elastic Search -------------------
- We will start indexing the data.

Indexing Data
Batman
2008

- So they developed Elastic Search tool.
- Where it indexed the data in JSON format so the retrieval, search or scanning process will be fast.  

-------------------------------------------------------

------------------------ Logstash ------------------------

- So when the application evolve technically the logs will be increase more
- and Logstash data will be saved in to the Elastic Search 
(Logstash -> ElasticSearch ES)  

-------------------------------------------------------

---------------- Kibana (Display or Visualization tool) -----------------

- And Kibana is one of the most popular log exploration and dashboard tools, but other platforms like Grafana, Splunk, and Datadog 
- Logstash -> ElasticSearch (ES) -> Kibana

-------------------------------------------------------

---------------- Beats -----------------

- New Update or Feature in Beats: Elastic Agents
- What Beats would do: Captures the containers, VMs, file system RAM, CPU, Network Latency.  

- Metrics: RAM, CPU, Files Uploaded, Network access
- Beats -> Logstash -> ElasticSearch (ES) -> Kibana
 

-------------------------------------------------------

- So ELK Stack is the old one and we have now Elastic Stack.